  "Notes": "Reference case: 55 A gold electrode directly on the prism, no cavity films\nSpecification: None (analysis case).\nReported: Table III, Au with no cavity: with absorption (n0 = 1.4 - i0.04) Rp = 0.236, Rs = 0.665; without absorption (n0 = 1.4 - i0.00) Rp = 0.865, Rs = 0.829. At 550 nm, 72.8 deg.\nNotes: Text: 'reflectances calculated with and without absorption for the gold electrode alone, i.e., with no cavity films intervening between it and the prism'. Gold thickness 0.010 lambda = 5.5 nm at 550 nm. The without-absorption case needs substrate {n: 1.4, k: 0}.\nLayers from Table III ('Au with no cavity'), p. 2113; gold film from Table II; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours Rp 0.236, Rs 0.665 at 72.8 deg, 550 nm; paper Rp 0.236, Rs 0.665 (Tables I and III).",
